ine's choice was D6, the point Black later took."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "E7 lost 13.5 points, the 20k's worst move, handing the lead back: Black's lead dropped from +20.1 to +6.6. The engine wanted F7 here."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "After D6 had pushed the score to Black -3.9, D8 lost 11.2 points and the lead went to +7.2. The engine's choice was H4, the point GPT-6.1 Sol only took at move 34."}, {"turn": 38, "text": "H5 lost 6.4 points, moving Black's lead from -2.6 to +3.8. After this White was never ahead again, and the 20k held the lead to the end."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "All the JavaScript ran was board parsing and group/liberty/area counting (the inspect function), a replay verifier that re-applies the moves actually played to check records, SGF conversion, and file reads/writes; every play call used a move the player chose directly. Nothing looped over candidate moves or looked ahead along continuations.", "stop": false}}